    "name": "Sea Lily",
    "name_ja": "トリノアシ",
    "scientific_name": "Metacrinus rotundus",
    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 73,
    "notes": "Stalked crinoid of the rocky and gravelly shelf edge off central Japan: a long, jointed, round-pentagonal stalk (30-50 cm) with whorls of five short, clawed cirri at intervals, a small cup-shaped calyx and a crown of five arms that branch 3-4 times into about 50 feathery arms fringed with pinnules, held open like a parabolic fan into the current 10-50 cm above the bottom. Pale reddish in life. Filter feeder; sheds its crown under stress and regrows it. No bioluminescence.",
